<title>JAPAN: Japan car stocks driven lower by ratings cut.</title>
<headline>Japan car stocks driven lower by ratings cut.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Toyota Motor Corp and Honda Motor Co Ltd skidded lower in Tuesday morning trade after a foreign brokerage cut the ratings of the two car makers overnight, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0036 GMT, Toyota was down 60 yen at 3,680. Turnover was 1.8 million shares, making it the 10th most heavily traded issue on the Tokyo bourse.</p>
<p>Honda had lost 170 yen to trade at 3,780.  </p>
<p>In New York on Monday, Morgan Stanley cut the ratings of the two firms from &quot;outperform&quot; to &quot;neutral&quot;.</p>
